   "name": "Instructions.pdf",
   "kind": "pdf",
   "min_pages": 3,
   "max_pages": 10,
   "required_headings": [
    "What's Included",
    "Getting Started",
    "Using Google Sheets",
    "Dashboard",
    "Jobs and Customers",
    "Expenses and Supplies",
    "Mileage Log",
    "Monthly Summary",
    "Tax Time Tips",
    "Important Notes"
   ],
   "title": "Mobile Auto Detailer Business Tracker",
   "footer": "Mobile Auto Detailer Business Tracker",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "p": "Instructions for the Mobile Detailer Business Tracker: one workbook for jobs, customers, expenses, supplies and mileage, with a Dashboard that shows how the business is doing. Built for one-person and small mobile detailing businesses that want clean records without accounting software."
    },
    {
     "heading": "What's Included"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "File",
       "What it is"
      ],
      [
       "Mobile_Detailer_Business_Tracker.xlsx",
       "The tracker workbook: Dashboard, Jobs, Expenses, Supplies, Mileage Log, Customers, Summary, IRS Rates and Lists tabs"
      ],
      [
       "Instructions.pdf",
       "This guide"
      ],
      [
       "README.txt",
       "A short quick-start note"
      ]
     ],
     "widths": [
      3.2,
      3.5
     ]
    },
    {
     "p": "The workbook's tabs:"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Tab",
       "What you do there"
      ],
      [
       "How to Use",
       "A one-page reminder of these steps"
      ],
      [
       "Dashboard",
       "Set the tax year and tax set-aside %; see key figures and three charts"
      ],
      [
       "Jobs",
       "Enter every job once: it counts as income and updates the customer's history"
      ],
      [
       "Expenses",
       "Business bills and purchases other than detailing supplies"
      ],
      [
       "Supplies",
       "Chemicals, towels, pads and equipment, with cost per job"
      ],
      [
       "Mileage Log",
       "Business trips and the IRS standard mileage deduction"
      ],
      [
       "Customers",
       "Contact details; visits, spend, unpaid balance and last visit fill in"
      ],
      [
       "Summary",
       "Month-by-month income, costs, profit and mileage"
      ],
      [
       "IRS Rates",
       "Standard mileage rates by date; add new ones here"
      ],
      [
       "Lists",
       "The choices in every dropdown"
      ]
     ],
     "widths": [
      1.5,
      5.2
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Getting Started"
    },
    {
     "bullets": [
      "Unzip the download and save the files to a folder you back up, such as OneDrive, Google Drive or Dropbox.",
      "Open Mobile_Detailer_Business_Tracker.xlsx in Microsoft Excel (2010 or newer, Windows or Mac). It opens on the **How to Use** tab.",
      "Go to the **Dashboard** and type your tax year and tax set-aside % in the yellow cells.",
      "Type only in white table cells and yellow cells. Grey cells hold formulas and calculate on their own.",
      "Enter dates as month/day/year, for example 3/15/2026, and amounts without a $ sign."
     ],
     "numbered": true
    },
    {
     "heading": "Using Google Sheets"
    },
    {
     "bullets": [
      "In Google Drive choose **New > File upload** and upload the .xlsx file.",
      "Open it, then choose **File > Save as Google Sheets** so edits save automatically.",
      "Formulas, dropdowns, frozen headers and the Dashboard charts carry over. Google Sheets may draw the charts with its own fonts and colors."
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Dashboard"
    },
    {
     "p": "The Dashboard is where you set up the year and check results. **Tax Year** decides which entries count. **Tax Set-Aside %** is the share of profit you want to put aside for taxes. Add your odometer readings on January 1 and December 31 to see total miles and your business-use percentage."
    },
    {
     "p": "Key figures: total income, total costs (expenses plus supplies), net profit and margin, the mileage deduction, **Profit After Mileage** (net profit minus the mileage deduction), the **Tax Set-Aside** amount, take-home after the set-aside, jobs completed and unpaid balances. The three charts show income against costs by month, profit after mileage by month, and costs by category."
    },
    {
     "p": "Nothing is set aside when profit after mileage is zero or negative. The tax set-aside is a savings target, not a tax calculation. Many self-employed people put aside 25-30% of profit; ask a tax professional what fits you."
    },
    {
     "p": "The chart axes count up in steps of $1,000. If your months run well above $15,000 and the axis labels look crowded, right-click the numbers on the axis, choose **Format Axis** and raise the **Major** unit (for example to 5000)."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Jobs and Customers"
    },
    {
     "p": "Add each customer once on the **Customers** tab. Then record every job on the **Jobs** tab, picking the customer from the dropdown so names match exactly. Enter the service amount and any tip; Total adds them. Mark **Paid?** Yes or No. That single row is your income record and also updates the customer's job count, total spent, unpaid balance and last visit, so there is no second log to keep. Sort Customers by Last Visit to find people due for a maintenance detail."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Expenses and Supplies"
    },
    {
     "p": "Use **Supplies** for detailing chemicals, towels, pads and equipment: quantity, unit and cost per unit, plus **Jobs per Unit** (how many jobs one bottle, gallon or pack lasts). Cost per Job shows what that supply costs you each time. Supplies count as costs automatically, so don't enter them on Expenses as well."
    },
    {
     "p": "Use **Expenses** for everything else: insurance, marketing, phone and software, licenses, water and so on. Pick a category so the Summary and Dashboard can total costs by category."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Mileage Log"
    },
    {
     "p": "Log every business trip: to a customer, between customers, to buy supplies or to the bank. Enter the date, purpose, where you went and the business miles. The log looks up the IRS standard mileage rate in effect on that date and calculates the deduction. Rates included on the **IRS Rates** tab:"
    },
    {
     "bullets": [
      "$0.70 per mile from January 1, 2025 (IRS Notice 2025-5)",
      "$0.725 per mile from January 1, 2026 (IRS Notice 2026-10)",
      "$0.76 per mile from July 1, 2026 (IRS Announcement 2026-11)"
     ]
    },
    {
     "p": "When the IRS announces a new rate, add a row to the IRS Rates tab with the date it takes effect. Keep the rows in date order, oldest first. A trip showing \"No rate\" is dated before the first rate listed."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Monthly Summary"
    },
    {
     "p": "The **Summary** tab shows income, expenses, supplies, net profit, mileage deduction and profit after mileage for each month of the Dashboard's tax year, with year totals. Beside it are costs by category and supplies by category. The Dashboard charts read from this tab."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Tax Time Tips"
    },
    {
     "bullets": [
      "Set the tax year on the Dashboard and give the totals to your tax preparer.",
      "Keep receipts for expenses and supplies. A tracker supports your records but doesn't replace them.",
      "Choose either the standard mileage rate or actual vehicle expenses for a vehicle, not both. If you use the mileage rate, don't also enter fuel and repairs for that vehicle as expenses.",
      "Back up the workbook regularly, and keep a copy of each finished year."
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Important Notes"
    },
    {
     "p": "This product is a record-keeping tool and is not tax advice. Tax rules change and depend on your situation; confirm deductions with a qualified tax professional or irs.gov."
    },
    {
     "p": "IRS mileage rates are included as published when this version was built. Check irs.gov for the current rate before filing."
    },
    {
     "p": "Customer contact details are personal information. Keep the workbook private and don't share it."
    }
   ]
